course: dictionary
lesson: 4014
title: Describing food with garlicky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can tell you how something tastes or smells. Garlicky means tasting or smelling strongly of garlic. Read the sentence around it to check. In the Rat's picnic, «a sausage out of which the garlic sang» tells you the smell is loud and strong.
explain: The word sang is a clue. Garlic cannot really sing, so the writer is describing a powerful smell in a playful way. Ask yourself: what would the food smell or taste like? If the answer is strong garlic, garlicky is the right meaning.
explain: Garlicky can also describe breath. If someone jokes about «garlicky breath», they mean their breath smells of garlic because they have just eaten some. Here the word is used in a light, funny way, not to be unkind.
explain: Like other describing words, garlicky has forms for comparing. You can say more garlicky to compare two dishes, and most garlicky to pick the strongest one. Use these when you want to say which of two or more foods is stronger in garlic.
fact: Garlicky means tasting or smelling strongly of garlic.
fact: Garlicky also means having breath that smells of garlic after eating it.
fact: Garlicky is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «garlicky bread».
fact: Its comparison forms are more garlicky and most garlicky.
fact: Garlicky dishes include garlic bread, some pasta sauces, and many dishes from Italy, France, Spain and Asia.
exercise: «The sauce was so garlicky that the whole kitchen smelled of it.» What does garlicky mean? | Quiet and still | Sweet, like sugar | Cold and wet from the rain | *Tasting or smelling strongly of garlic
exercise: In «a sausage out of which the garlic sang», what does sang suggest? | *The garlic smell was loud and strong | The garlic was singing a song | The garlic was hidden under the bread | The sausage was cooked for a long time
exercise: Mum says, «Your breath is garlicky after the pasta.» What does she mean? | Your breath has no smell at all | *Your breath smells of garlic because you ate some | Your breath is very slow | Your breath is very cold
test: «He joked about his garlicky breath after the pizza.» What does garlicky breath mean? | Breath that is very cold | Breath that is hard to hear | Breath that is sweet like fruit | *Breath that smells of garlic after eating it
test: Which sentence uses the correct form of garlicky to compare two soups? | The second soup was garlicky than the first | The second soup was garlickyer than the first | *The second soup was more garlicky than the first | The second soup was most garlicky than the first
exam: Which of these is a garlicky dish? | A glass of cold milk | A dry biscuit | A bowl of plain fruit salad | *Garlic bread
